{
"prog": "modify",
"name": "stack",
"mode": 0,
"cat": "pitch",
"title": "Stack",
"short": "Stack transposed copies on top of each other: instant chords",
"about": "This process takes the sound and makes numerous copies of it, set by the number of layers. Each copy is sped up or slowed down by the transposition amount multiplied  by its layer number - -12 semitones = half speed, +12 semitones = double speed. These layers are then stacks on top of each other to create a denser sound. The attack offset is used to line up the layers so that their attacks all line up, adjust this to the point in the input where you want all the sounds to line up. The output duration allows you to trim off the end of the sound as with negative transposition and many layers the output can get very long.",
"credit": "SoundThread"
},
