"about": "This process goes through all the input sounds and for each channel in the analysis it retains only the single loudest spectral component among all the input files in each window. This produces an effect similar to mixing the sounds together but with some spectral morphing and interaction between them. This generally works best with sounds that have similar dynamic but varied spectral content.",
